cff-version: 1.2.0
title: ATRIA EchoTrace
message: >-
  If you use this software or the released adapters, please cite the software and the
  DEITY Principles Framework paper below. The underlying datasets carry their own
  citation requirements — see the references section.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Anwer
    given-names: Shehab
    name-suffix: MD
    affiliation: The Adimension
repository-code: https://github.com/The-Adimension/ATRIA-EchoTrace
abstract: >-
  ATRIA EchoTrace fine-tunes MedGemma 1.5 4B with QLoRA to emit the left-ventricular
  endocardial border as an ordered JSON list of 30 boundary points normalised to a
  [0, 1000] grid, rather than as a segmentation mask. Because the output is editable
  structure, a clinician's correction can be captured and fed back as training data.
  Research use only; not a cleared or approved medical device.
keywords:
  - echocardiography
  - medical-imaging
  - MedGemma
  - QLoRA
  - structured-output
  - human-in-the-loop
  - HAI-DEF
license: Apache-2.0

references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      The Adimension: bridging human ingenuity and machine intelligence through
      the DEITY principles framework
    authors:
      - family-names: Anwer
        given-names: Shehab
    journal: European Heart Journal — Imaging Methods and Practice
    volume: 4
    issue: 1
    year: 2025
    doi: 10.1093/ehjimp/qyaf038
    notes: Article number qyaf038.

  - type: software
    title: EchoTrace-MedGemma-CAMUS (LoRA adapter)
    authors:
      - family-names: Anwer
        given-names: Shehab
    doi: 10.57967/hf/9541
    license: Apache-2.0

  - type: software
    title: EchoTrace-MedGemma-EchoNet (LoRA adapter)
    authors:
      - family-names: Anwer
